# HVACPulse

Kafka → Spark Structured Streaming → Delta medallion, plus a mock plant loop.
Advisory/mock control only. Python ≥3.10 (CI 3.11), uv, PySpark 3.5.5,
delta-spark 3.2.1, Kafka 3.9.1. Java 17 for Spark.

## Commands

```powershell
uv sync --group dev --group dashboard
uv run ruff check .
uv run pytest tests/unit -m unit
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe contracts\check_compatibility.py contracts\avro
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe contracts\check_compatibility.py contracts\plant
.\scripts\local\run_local_stack.ps1 -Task all
.\scripts\local\run_local_stack.ps1 -Task plant-all
```

Spark, Delta, dashboard, and bundle commands stay in the scoped rules.

## Profiles and targets

- Local Delta: `HVACPULSE_DATA_ROOT` (default `.local/`).
- Kafka topic `hvac.telemetry` at `127.0.0.1:19092` (container `hvacpulse-kafka`).
- Bundle targets: `dev` (default) and `prod`. UC defaults: catalog
  `hvacpulse_dev`, schema `streaming`.
- Two profiles, one topic: air-handler Avro (`contracts/avro/`) and plant
  snapshots (`contracts/plant/`, header `event_type=plant_snapshot`).

## Do not commit

`.local/`, `terraform.tfvars`, `*.tfstate*`, `.env`, `*.pem`, `spark-warehouse/`.
Limits live in `reference/`, not in code. No dbt, Soda, or Great Expectations.

## Traps

- Do not set `SPARK_LOCAL_IP` on Windows. `create_spark` pops it; CI sets it
  only on Linux. OneDrive locks Delta in the repo — point
  `HVACPULSE_DATA_ROOT` outside OneDrive (example `C:\Temp\hvacpulse-local`).
- Event Hub name is `hvac-telemetry`. The local topic is `hvac.telemetry`.
- `create_spark` returns an active Databricks session unchanged.
